Rule 1 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (tensor shape matches given tuple shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = v_2.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = v_2[i]
>>
Rule 3 (index tensor (v_2) should be within the range of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_1, i) - 1
>>
Rule 4 (primitive type variable must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 6 (tensor should not contain NaN values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : max(v_1) ≠ NaN
>>
Rule 7 (tensor should not contain inf values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : max(v_1) ≠ Inf
>>
Rule 9 (tensor should not contain out-of-range values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : max(v_1) < 1 ∧ min(v_1) > -1
